    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** lineup for July 1st is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (78.03) and **Kyle Tucker** (77.94), our two highest-rated starters. **Gunnar Henderson** faces a prime matchup against Schultz, whose 5.16 xERA is the highest on our board, and despite the slight negative adjustment for the platoon, the significant park and skill advantages make him an elite start. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Ginn, with his score bolstered by strong park factors and a favorable batting order position. **Jackson Merrill** also provides elite value (75.27) today; his aggressive platoon edge against Rea and the high-upside matchup context make him a cornerstone of the outfield production.\n\nOur most critical bench decision involved **Miguel Vargas** (48.65), who remained on the outside looking in despite an elite 0.407 xwOBA. While his park factors in the matchup against Kremer were high, the significant skill of the opposing pitcher (-19% SP Skill impact) and the overall depth of the starting roster squeezed him out of the UTIL and backup infield slots. Elsewhere, we are monitoring the SB risk for **Nasim Nunez**; while he is in the lineup, he faces a tough \"Elite Hold\" pitcher, which creates a slight headwind for his stolen base probability. **Liam Hicks** also enters the day with a lower-than-average score of 49.45, heavily impacted by the platoon disadvantage against Freeland, though he remains in the lineup to maintain roster efficiency. \n\nAs we manage our game caps, we are keeping a close eye on **Jordan Westburg**, who remains sidelined on the IL. Today\u2019s lineup prioritizes high-floor performers like **Andy Pages** (70.62) and **Drake Baldwin** (65.60), who offer stable contributions against mid-tier pitching. We have avoided any high-risk weather scenarios, though investors should note that **Nasim Nunez** and **Coby Mayo** are facing \"Elite Hold\" SPs, meaning we aren't banking on a stolen base windfall from those spots. We will evaluate performance closely to see if **Miguel Vargas** or **Brayan Rocchio** should be rotated in for the following series if today's marginal starters underperform.",
